धा
धा (लि, ञ, डु) दधाति, ते 3.<BR>c. To hold<BR>or support; to nurture; to have.<BR>With अभि to cover, to address;<BR>with अव to take heed; with आ^1 to<BR>receive; with उप^2 to uphold, to per-<BR>form; with नि^3 to hold up, to place;<BR>with परि^4 to put on cloths; with प्र^5 to be<BR>chief, to send; with वि^6 act correctly,<BR>to select; with सं^7 to place. With अनु<BR>and सं to search after; with अभि^8 and<BR>सं to overcome; with उप^9 and आ to<BR>support or prop up; with प्र^10 and नि<BR>to hold up, to elevate; with प्रति^11 and<BR>वि to perform; with वि^12 and अव to<BR>conceal; with सं^13 and आ to instruct;<BR>with सं and नि to place or have over;<BR>with सं and प्र to doubt, to discuss.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[3] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[4] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[5] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[6] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[7] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[8] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[9] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[10] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[11] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[12] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[13] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=YAT&page=393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=yat" target="_blank">Correction</a>

