पद्
पद् (य, ङ, औ) पद्यते 4.<BR>d. To go (क)<BR>पदयति 10.<BR>a. Idem. (ए) पदति<BR>1.<BR>a. To stand fast. With अभि<BR>to know, to see; with अनु^1 to follow;<BR>with आ^2 to happen, suffer, increase;<BR>with उत्^3 to be born or produced;<BR>with उप^4 to gain, be born; with प्र^5 to gain,<BR>begin; with प्रति^6 to gain; restore;<BR>promise; with वि^7 to suffer; with सं^8 to<BR>perform, do; with उप^9 and with सं^10 to<BR>offer oblations; with प्र^11 and with वि^12 to en-<BR>act; with वि^13 and with आ^14 to kill; with वि^15 and<BR>with उत्^16 to discriminate, analyze; with सं^17<BR>and with आ^18 to arrive, finish.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[3] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[4] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[5] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[6] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[7] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[8] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[9] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[10] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[11] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[12] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[13] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[14] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[15] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[16] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[17] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR>[18] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20200322. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/202.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=YAT&page=446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=yat" target="_blank">Correction</a>

